- adv-souda-appearance: The unqualified adjective rule omits standalone ない → なさそう. The same rule applied to かわいい produces かわいそう but that means pitiable, not looks cute. These are explicit exceptions/traps in the cited source. Corrected payload SHA256: 9cce97689c03bb42c90fd4d2c91704d6f70bccfb6bfcfb3721609a500c96cd37. (13 October 2026)
